# track_payoff.py writes one intermediate CSV per arm and one candidate-build
# log directory per arm into its --results-dir before combining them. They are
# runner state, not results: committing them puts files in the provenance table
# that no declared job produced, so the page reports them as unverified and the
# whole table stops meaning anything. Sixteen of twenty-six rows read
# "unverified" before this was added.
#
# The regeneration entrypoint runs each job into a temporary directory and
# stages only its declared outputs, so nothing here is needed for a normal run.
# This catches a script pointed straight at data/ by hand.
_payoff_*.csv
logs-*/
